WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.117
This model follows one real, published case.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:07.243
A man aged 42 had a slow-growing lump in the roof of his mouth.

00:00:07.593 --> 00:00:10.900
It was a slow type of cancer that starts in a small spit gland.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.671
The surgeon took out the lump with a cuff of normal lining,

00:00:14.671 --> 00:00:16.031
and kept the bone above it.

00:00:16.831 --> 00:00:19.604
He lost no teeth, and there was no hole into the nose.

00:00:20.404 --> 00:00:23.775
A clear plastic plate protected the area while new lining grew.

00:00:24.575 --> 00:00:28.628
By 4 months the roof of the mouth had healed. He then had regular checks.
